      "writtenOn": "2021-04-22T15:24:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I found this confusing - the actual bus is I2C 7, but the enum references I2C0.  I think you should create new enums GPIO_EC_I2C_SENSOR_SCL and GPIO_EC_I2C_SENSOR_SDA.\n\nAnother thought is to change this child-binding to point to a gpio phandle-array instead of the enum.  Then use the DT macros to extract the gpio-enum-name.\n\nExample here: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/793c8e2f/zephyr/dts/bindings/retimer/intel,jhl8040r.yaml#\n\nThis could be done in the same CL that removes the frequency property from the tree.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 82,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 82,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "b46844ced866c9e4a2b61a73321a9569bef5c615",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9ca38685_86c40d1d",
        "filename": "zephyr/projects/trogdor/boards/arm/trogdor/trogdor.dts",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 82,
